From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0405-upscale-square-packed-frame.patch

Source: 0405-upscale-square-packed-frame.patch
frame (EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SQUARE)

Ocarina of Time's network reads one 1920x1080 E5B9G9R9 image (cbuf0+0xc0) and stores one
B10G11R11 image (+0xd0), run81 and run82. With its HMMA rejected, the stand-in copies the first
to the second as it stands. Run83 is that copy: a pale world, fog score median 77 ("same-size
copy 0x8113971000 format 32 1920x1080 -> 0x81252ff000 format 33", "plain copy").

Lichii PR 143 (open, Intel Arc, Mesa ANV, nothing measured on AMD) reports the same pair in the
same slots, and that the image holds the square root of each tonemapped channel: against the
pass that writes the tonemapped frame it fits gamma 2.0, scale 1.00, median error 0.0002. The
network squares it back, so a plain copy shows 0.25 as 0.5, a white haze. Its SrcCopySquare and
blit_color_square.frag are taken over as they stand, so a later merge stays clean.

EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SQUARE=1: a stand-in copy whose source is E5B9G9R9 squares each colour channel,
logged once per program ("Upscale fallback for program ...: squares its E5B9G9R9 input"). Every
other source keeps its operation. Unset: the same operation as before on every copy. The only
difference is one small shader module created at start and never used.

This is the one test left from the E5B9G9R9 idea (console/notes/e5-white-hypothesis.md). The file
name is the one that idea was given: no render target format changes here. The core never asks
for E5B9G9R9 as a colour target (maxwell_to_vk.cpp:219), and the driver refuses it anyway.

Expect less white, not none. Squaring run83's captured frames offline took the fog median from
77 to 58, against 30 on Linux, and PR 143 still sees haze outdoors. Whether our image holds
square roots has not been measured.

Checked: applies after 0001-0404 and after black-world-06. Clang syntax check, PS5 target, no
warnings: kepler_compute.cpp, blit_image.cpp, fermi_2d.cpp, vk_texture_cache.cpp, with five
shader headers unrelated to this stubbed. The shader compiles with the build's glslangValidator
flags and passes spirv-val. Not built, not run.

